      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 402600691,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I think they should be in a consistent location, which is next to the extcap binary as this works with the current code for both global and personal extcaps.\n\nI think the only concern with having things other than the extcap binary in the extcap dir was that the code might attempt to execute them as if they were extcap binaries.  I didn't see any evidence of this.  I ran ProcMon while starting Wireshark and although it enumerates the ciscodump.html file as it's in the extcap directory it didn't do anything else with it, unlike the extcap binaries.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6621762,
            "username": "graham.bloice",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Graham Bloice",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
