    {
      "id": "3d395d91aeb2ea850e70a35b4033665380e6e967",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 402714284,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Probably not.  Linux, and other platforms, have well defined places to put data and docs, Windows doesn't.\n\nIMHO we either move the .html to the place that currently works or we invent a new directory layout for Windows, e.g. have a docs directory relative to the global or personal Wireshark directory and then fix up the installers and code to work with that and then get 3rd party extcap developers to also follow the new guidelines.",
